# Project Standards

- Keep `up` small, boring, and self-hosting-friendly.
- Use TypeScript for all project code.
- Use pnpm only. Keep `pnpm-lock.yaml` committed.
- Keep pnpm `minimumReleaseAge` set to 2880 minutes.
- Prefer correctness, durability, and simple operations over cloud-scale abstractions.
- Do not implement deferred features while doing setup-only tasks.
- Add comments only when they clarify non-obvious logic.
- Keep route handlers thin once API routes exist.
- Preserve local filesystem and SQLite assumptions unless user explicitly changes architecture.
